@startuml sequence-communication-chat
title CoreChain Communication - Chat Flow (WebSocket + REST API)

actor "Employee" as Employee
participant "Client App" as Client
participant "Communication\nService (Go)" as CommService
participant "JWT Auth\nMiddleware" as Auth
participant "WebSocket\nUpgrader" as WSUpgrader
participant "Hub" as Hub
participant "Client\nConnection" as WSClient
participant "ChatService" as ChatService
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "User Service\n(NestJS)" as UserService

== WebSocket Connection Establishment ==

Employee -> Client: Open chat
Client -> CommService: GET /ws?token=<JWT>
CommService -> Auth: Validate JWT token
Auth -> Auth: Parse and verify token\nwith JWT secret
Auth --> CommService: User claims\n(_id, role, name)

CommService -> WSUpgrader: Upgrade HTTP to WebSocket
WSUpgrader --> CommService: WebSocket connection

CommService -> WSClient: Create client instance\n(userID, conn, send channel)
CommService -> Hub: Register client
activate Hub
Hub -> Hub: Add client to clients map\n(userID -> client)
Hub --> CommService: Client registered
deactivate Hub

CommService -> WSClient: Start WritePump() goroutine
CommService -> WSClient: Start ReadPump() goroutine

note right of WSClient
  **Hub Pattern**
  - Maintains active connections
  - Routes messages to recipients
  - Handles broadcast logic
end note

== Send Message via WebSocket ==

Employee -> Client: Type and send message
Client -> WSClient: WebSocket message\n{"type":"send", "conversation_id":123,\n"content":"Hello", "receiver_id":"456"}

WSClient -> Hub: Forward message
activate Hub
Hub -> ChatService: CreateMessage(ctx, params)
ChatService -> DB: INSERT INTO messages\n(conversation_id, sender_id,\ncontent, created_at)
DB --> ChatService: Message ID

ChatService -> DB: UPDATE conversations\nSET last_message, updated_at
DB --> ChatService: Updated

ChatService --> Hub: Message created

Hub -> Hub: Find recipient client\nby receiver_id
Hub -> WSClient: Send to recipient's\nsend channel
WSClient -> Client: WebSocket push\n(new message)
Client -> Employee: Display message
deactivate Hub

note right of Hub
  **Real-time Broadcasting**
  If recipient is online, 
  message is pushed via WebSocket.
  Otherwise, it's stored in DB
  for later retrieval.
end note

== REST API: Create/Get Private Conversation ==

Employee -> Client: Start new conversation
Client -> CommService: POST /conversations/private\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\n{"partner_id": "456"}

CommService -> Auth: WithAuth middleware
Auth -> Auth: Validate JWT
Auth --> CommService: Set user_id in context

CommService -> ChatService: GetOrCreatePrivateConversation\n(userID, partnerID)
ChatService -> DB: SELECT * FROM conversations\nWHERE is_group=false\nAND participants @> [user_id, partner_id]

alt Conversation exists
  DB --> ChatService: Conversation record
else Conversation doesn't exist
  ChatService -> DB: INSERT INTO conversations\n(is_group, created_by,\nparticipants, created_at)
  DB --> ChatService: New conversation ID
end

ChatService -> ChatService: GetConversation(conversationID)
ChatService -> DB: SELECT conversation with\nlast message details
DB --> ChatService: Conversation detail

ChatService -> UserService: GET /users?ids=[user_id, partner_id]
UserService --> ChatService: User details\n(name, avatar, etc.)

ChatService -> ChatService: Enrich conversation\nwith user details
ChatService --> CommService: Conversation object

CommService --> Client: 200 OK\n{"data": {"id": 123,\n"participants": [...],\n"last_message": {...}}}
Client -> Employee: Show conversation

== REST API: List Conversations ==

Employee -> Client: View all chats
Client -> CommService: GET /conversations\n?limit=20&offset=0\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>

CommService -> Auth: WithAuth middleware
Auth --> CommService: user_id in context

CommService -> ChatService: ListConversations\n(userID, limit, offset)
ChatService -> DB: SELECT * FROM conversations\nWHERE user_id = ANY(participants)\nORDER BY updated_at DESC\nLIMIT 20 OFFSET 0

DB --> ChatService: Conversation list

ChatService -> UserService: Batch get user details\nfor all participants
UserService --> ChatService: User details map

ChatService -> ChatService: Enrich each conversation\nwith user info and\nlast message
ChatService --> CommService: Conversations array

CommService --> Client: 200 OK\n{"data": [conversations]}
Client -> Employee: Display chat list

== REST API: Get Messages ==

Employee -> Client: View message history
Client -> CommService: GET /messages\n?conversation_id=123&limit=50\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>

CommService -> Auth: WithAuth middleware
Auth --> CommService: user_id authenticated

CommService -> ChatService: GetMessages\n(conversationID, limit, offset)
ChatService -> DB: SELECT * FROM messages\nWHERE conversation_id = 123\nORDER BY created_at DESC\nLIMIT 50

DB --> ChatService: Messages array

ChatService -> UserService: Get sender details\nfor each message
UserService --> ChatService: User details

ChatService -> ChatService: Enrich messages with\nsender information
ChatService --> CommService: Messages with details

CommService --> Client: 200 OK\n{"data": [messages]}
Client -> Employee: Display message history

== Client Disconnection ==

Employee -> Client: Close app/navigate away
Client -> WSClient: Close WebSocket
WSClient -> Hub: Unregister client
Hub -> Hub: Remove client from\nclients map
Hub --> WSClient: Client removed

note right of Hub
  **Connection Cleanup**
  When a client disconnects,
  the Hub removes it from
  active connections to
  prevent memory leaks.
end note

@enduml
